  "before_interfaces": {
    "lem-it-finite-gentle-measurement": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\rho$ be a density operator on a nonzero finite-dimensional complex inner-product space $H$, let $0\\preceq\\Lambda\\preceq I_H$, and suppose $\\operatorname{tr}(\\Lambda\\rho)\\ge1-u$ for some $u\\in[0,1]$. Then\n\n$$\\left\\|\\rho-\\sqrt{\\Lambda}\\rho\\sqrt{\\Lambda}\\right\\|_1\\le2\\sqrt{u}.$$\n\nHere $\\sqrt{\\Lambda}$ is the unique nonnegative square root, and $\\|\\cdot\\|_1$ is the finite-dimensional trace norm. No normalization is applied after the operation $\\rho\\mapsto\\sqrt{\\Lambda}\\rho\\sqrt{\\Lambda}$."
    ],
    "lem-it-finite-positive-square-root-is-order-preserving": [
      "## Statement\n\nIf $A,B$ are nonnegative endomorphisms of a nonzero finite-dimensional complex inner-product space and $A\\preceq B$, then their nonnegative square roots satisfy $A^{1/2}\\preceq B^{1/2}$."
    ],
    "lem-it-hayashi-nagaoka-finite-operator-inequality": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $S,T$ be nonnegative endomorphisms of a finite-dimensional complex inner-product space $H$, with $S\\preceq I_H$. Define $(S+T)^{-1/2}$ spectrally on $\\operatorname{supp}(S+T)$ and set it to zero on $\\ker(S+T)$. Then\n\n$$I_H-(S+T)^{-1/2}S(S+T)^{-1/2}\\preceq2(I_H-S)+4T.$$"
    ],
    "def-it-quantum-source-and-compression-code": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $H_A$ be a nonzero finite-dimensional complex inner-product space and let $\\rho$ be a density operator ([[def-qc-density-operator]]) on $H_A$. The finite IID quantum source with state $\\rho$ emits the block state $\\rho^{\\otimes n}$ on $H_A^{\\otimes n}$ at blocklength $n\\ge1$.\n\nAn $(n,M)$ **quantum compression code** for $\\rho$ consists of a finite-dimensional code space $H_C$ with $\\dim H_C=M\\ge1$, a quantum channel ([[def-qc-quantum-channel]]) $\\mathcal E:\\mathcal L(H_A^{\\otimes n})\\to\\mathcal L(H_C)$, and a quantum channel $\\mathcal D:\\mathcal L(H_C)\\to\\mathcal L(H_A^{\\otimes n})$. Its **squared entanglement fidelity** is\n\n$$F_e^{(n)}:=\\langle\\phi|(\\operatorname{id}_R\\otimes(\\mathcal D\\circ\\mathcal E))(|\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi|)|\\phi\\rangle,$$\n\nwhere $H_R$ is any finite-dimensional reference space supporting the chosen unit-vector purification $|\\phi\\rangle$ of $\\rho^{\\otimes n}$ on $H_R\\otimes H_A^{\\otimes n}$. The value is independent of the chosen finite purification by the isometric equivalence of [[thm-qc-purification-existence-and-unitary-equivalence]]. A sequence of codes is reliable when $F_e^{(n)}\\to1$. The code's rate is $n^{-1}\\ln M$ nats per source letter, equivalently $n^{-1}\\log_2 M$ qubits per source letter. The entropy threshold in these units is $S(\\rho)$ nats or $S_2(\\rho):=S(\\rho)/\\ln2$ qubits, where $S$ is the entropy of [[def-it-von-neumann-entropy]]."
    ],
    "lem-it-finite-quantum-entropy-continuity": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor each fixed finite dimension $d$, von Neumann entropy is continuous on density operators ([[def-qc-density-operator]]) on $\\mathbb C^d$ in operator norm ([[def-operator-norm-on-a-finite-dimensional-inner-product-space]]). Thus, if $\\rho_k\\to\\rho$ in operator norm, then $S(\\rho_k)\\to S(\\rho)$."
    ],
    "lem-it-square-root-cq-packing-bound": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\mathcal X$ be a finite nonempty set, let $p$ be a probability vector, and let $\\sigma_x$ be density operators on a finite-dimensional $H$. Let $\\bar\\sigma=\\sum_xp_x\\sigma_x$. Suppose that for every $x$ in the support of $p$, projections $\\Pi,\\Pi_x$ satisfy\n$$\\operatorname{tr}(\\Pi\\sigma_x)\\ge1-u,\\quad \\operatorname{tr}(\\Pi_x\\sigma_x)\\ge1-u,\\quad \\operatorname{rank}\\Pi_x\\le d,$$\nand $\\Pi\\bar\\sigma\\Pi\\preceq D^{-1}\\Pi$, where $u\\in[0,1]$ and $d,D>0$. For $M\\ge1$, draw $X_1,\\ldots,X_M$ independently with law $p$. Then the square-root POVM built from $\\Gamma_m=\\Pi\\Pi_{X_m}\\Pi$ has expected average error at most\n$$2(u+2\\sqrt{u})+4(M-1)\\frac dD.$$"
    ],
    "lem-it-schmidt-rank-compression-fidelity-bound": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\rho^{\\otimes n}$ have decreasing eigenvalues $\\lambda_1^{(n)}\\ge\\lambda_2^{(n)}\\ge\\cdots\\ge0$, padded by zeros, and let an $(n,M)$ compression code have intermediate dimension $M$ as in [[def-it-quantum-source-and-compression-code]]. Then\n\n$$F_e^{(n)}\\le\\sum_{j=1}^{M}\\lambda_j^{(n)}.$$"
    ],
    "def-it-classical-quantum-memoryless-channel": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $\\mathcal X$ be a finite nonempty input alphabet and let $H_B$ be a nonzero finite-dimensional complex inner-product space. A **finite-input cq channel** is a map $x\\mapsto\\rho_x$ assigning a density operator ([[def-qc-density-operator]]) $\\rho_x$ on $H_B$ to each $x\\in\\mathcal X$. Its $n$-use memoryless extension sends a word $x^n=(x_1,\\ldots,x_n)$ to the product state\n$$\\rho_{x^n}:=\\rho_{x_1}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes\\rho_{x_n}\\quad\\text{on }H_B^{\\otimes n}.$$\nFor an input probability vector $p$, write $\\bar\\rho_p=\\sum_xp_x\\rho_x$ and $\\chi_p=S(\\bar\\rho_p)-\\sum_{x:p_x>0}p_xS(\\rho_x)$; this is the Holevo information of the ensemble in [[def-it-classical-quantum-state-and-holevo-information]], in nats."
    ],
    "def-it-cq-channel-block-code-and-error": [
      "## Definition\n\nFix a finite-input cq channel as in [[def-it-classical-quantum-memoryless-channel]]. For integers $n,M\\ge1$, an $(n,M)$ **cq block code** consists of a deterministic encoder $m\\mapsto x^n(m)\\in\\mathcal X^n$ for $m\\in[M]:=\\{1,\\ldots,M\\}$ and a finite POVM ([[def-qc-povm-and-outcome-law]]) $(\\Lambda_m)_{m\\in[M]}$ on $H_B^{\\otimes n}$. Under a uniform message, its **average block error** is\n$$e_n:=\\frac1M\\sum_{m=1}^M\\left(1-\\operatorname{tr}(\\Lambda_m\\rho_{x^n(m)})\\right).$$\nIts rate is $n^{-1}\\ln M$ nats per channel use, using the natural-log unit convention of [[def-it-von-neumann-entropy]]. A sequence of such codes is reliable if $e_n\\to0$. The **classical capacity** $C_{\\rm cq}$ is the supremum of $\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}n^{-1}\\ln M_n$ over reliable sequences.\n\nFor each transmitted state, the POVM outcome weights sum to one by [[thm-qc-povm-probabilities-normalize]], so $e_n$ is the uniform-message block error probability."
    ],
    "lem-it-cq-typical-projector-dimension": [
      "## Statement\n\nAll logarithms are natural. First, for every density operator $\\rho$ on a nonzero finite-dimensional space and every $\\delta>0$, there are spectral projectors $\\Pi_n$ for $\\rho^{\\otimes n}$ such that, as $n\\to\\infty$,\n$$\\operatorname{tr}(\\Pi_n\\rho^{\\otimes n})\\to1,\\qquad \\operatorname{rank}\\Pi_n\\le e^{n(S(\\rho)+\\delta)},\\qquad \\Pi_n\\rho^{\\otimes n}\\Pi_n\\preceq e^{-n(S(\\rho)-\\delta)}\\Pi_n.$$\n\nSecond, let $\\mathcal X$ be a finite nonempty set, let $(p_x)_{x\\in\\mathcal X}$ be a probability vector, and let $\\sigma_x$ be density operators on a nonzero finite-dimensional output space. Put $\\bar\\sigma=\\sum_xp_x\\sigma_x$ and $H(B|X)=\\sum_{x:p_x>0}p_xS(\\sigma_x)$. For every $\\delta>0$, there are sets $T_n\\subseteq\\mathcal X^n$ with $p^{\\otimes n}(T_n)\\to1$, global spectral projectors $\\Pi_n$ for $\\bar\\sigma^{\\otimes n}$, and conditional spectral projectors $\\Pi_{x^n}$ for $\\bigotimes_i\\sigma_{x_i}$, such that one sequence $u_n\\to0$ satisfies, for every sufficiently large $n$ and every $x^n\\in T_n$,\n$$\\operatorname{tr}(\\Pi_n\\bar\\sigma^{\\otimes n})\\to1,\\quad \\operatorname{tr}(\\Pi_n\\bigotimes_i\\sigma_{x_i})\\ge1-u_n,\\quad \\operatorname{tr}(\\Pi_{x^n}\\bigotimes_i\\sigma_{x_i})\\ge1-u_n,$$\n$$\\operatorname{rank}\\Pi_n\\le e^{n(S(\\bar\\sigma)+\\delta)},\\quad \\Pi_n\\bar\\sigma^{\\otimes n}\\Pi_n\\preceq e^{-n(S(\\bar\\sigma)-\\delta)}\\Pi_n,$$\n$$\\operatorname{rank}\\Pi_{x^n}\\le e^{n(H(B|X)+\\delta)},\\quad \\Pi_{x^n}\\left(\\bigotimes_i\\sigma_{x_i}\\right)\\Pi_{x^n}\\preceq e^{-n(H(B|X)-\\delta)}\\Pi_{x^n}.$$\nZero eigenvalues are omitted from surprisal sums. No identical-distribution assumption is made for the conditional eigenbasis measurements."
    ],
    "thm-it-schumacher-quantum-source-coding": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\rho$ be a density operator on a nonzero finite-dimensional source space, and use the squared entanglement-fidelity code model of [[def-it-quantum-source-and-compression-code]]. Write $S(\\rho)$ in nats.\n\n1. For every $R>S(\\rho)$ there is a sequence of compression codes with $F_e^{(n)}\\to1$ and $\\limsup_n n^{-1}\\ln M_n\\le R$.\n2. If a sequence of codes satisfies $\\limsup_n n^{-1}\\ln M_n<S(\\rho)$, then $F_e^{(n)}\\to0$.\n\nThus the asymptotic reliable compression rate is exactly $S(\\rho)$ nats per source letter, or $S(\\rho)/\\ln2$ qubits per source letter."
    ],
    "thm-it-hsw-classical-quantum-channel-capacity": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $x\\mapsto\\rho_x$ be a finite-input, finite-output memoryless cq channel as in [[def-it-classical-quantum-memoryless-channel]]. With the average-error code convention of [[def-it-cq-channel-block-code-and-error]], its classical capacity in nats per use is\n$$C_{\\rm cq}=\\max_{p\\in\\Delta(\\mathcal X)}\\chi_p,\\qquad \\chi_p:=S\\!\\left(\\sum_xp_x\\rho_x\\right)-\\sum_{x:p_x>0}p_xS(\\rho_x).$$\nFor every $0\\le R<C_{\\rm cq}$ a sequence of codes with rate tending to $R$ has average error tending to zero, and every reliable sequence has limiting upper rate at most $C_{\\rm cq}$. This theorem concerns a fixed finite classical input alphabet and does not assert a single-letter formula for general quantum-input channels."
    ],
    "ex-it-qubit-source-compression": [],
    "cex-it-ensemble-holevo-information-is-not-measured-by-a-fixed-povm": [],
    "ex-it-cq-binary-pure-state-channel": []
  }
